Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:08:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Leave layers out of render passes without attachments.

Direct3D 12 can draw without render targets, for passes that only write
UAVs, such as Unreal's distance field shadows that scatter objects into
light tiles. vkd3d-proton then begins rendering with the largest render
area and layer count the device allows, and MoltenVK set that layer
count, 2048, as the render target array length of the Metal pass. The
GPU fails such a pass with an internal error, and the device is lost, as
in Medieval Dynasty a minute or two into its world. Without attachments
nothing uses layers, so only set them for passes with attachments or
multiview.
---
 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm
index de39c961..7f4c47c0 100644
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Commands/MVKCommandBuffer.mm
@@ -804,7 +804,13 @@ void MVKCommandEncoder::beginMetalRenderPass(MVKCommandUse cmdUse) {
 	VkExtent2D raFullExtent = { _renderArea.offset.x + _renderArea.extent.width, _renderArea.offset.y + _renderArea.extent.height };
     mtlRPDesc.renderTargetWidth = max(min(raFullExtent.width, (fbExtent.width ? fbExtent.width : raFullExtent.width)), 1u);
     mtlRPDesc.renderTargetHeight = max(min(raFullExtent.height, (fbExtent.height ? fbExtent.height : raFullExtent.height)), 1u);
-    if (_canUseLayeredRendering) {
+    // Without attachments, nothing needs layers, and layer counts as large as
+    // maxFramebufferLayers, which vkd3d-proton uses then, make the GPU fail the pass.
+    bool hasAttachments = mtlRPDesc.depthAttachment.texture || mtlRPDesc.stencilAttachment.texture;
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < 8 && !hasAttachments; i++) {
+        hasAttachments = mtlRPDesc.colorAttachments[i].texture != nil;
+    }
+    if (_canUseLayeredRendering && (hasAttachments || getSubpass()->isMultiview())) {
         uint32_t renderTargetArrayLength;
         bool found3D = false, found2D = false;
         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
